nts Veterans International Students Transfer Students Virtual Tour Research Arrow left icon Back Research at Fordham Faculty Research Student Research Digital Humanities Journals Published at Fordham Research Resources Office of Research Office of Sponsored Programs Institutional Review Board Libraries Quick Links Centers and Institutes Louis Calder Center Biological Field Station NYC Research Partners Related Links Research News Calder Center NYC Partners Libraries Student Life Arrow left icon Back Campus Culture Living on Campus Dining and Ram Hospitality Safety, Health, and Wellness Multicultural Affairs Public Safety Services Commuter Services Disability Services Career Resources Transportation Get Involved Events and Activities Student Involvement Student Organizations Quicklinks Student Handbook Bookstore Deans of Students and Student Life Division of Student Affairs Related Links Bookstore Commuter Services Residential Life Dining Student Handbook Resources Arrow left icon Back Resources Libraries Information Technology Human Resources Administrative Offices Hidden Public Safety WFUV Fordham University Press Fordham Antiquities Museum Hidden Log In Fordham News Policies Consumer Information Related Links Academic Calendar Jobs at Fordham Athletics Arrow left icon Back Athletics Varsity Sports Club Sports Hidden Intramurals Athletics Facilities Related Links Tickets Maroon Club Varsity Sports Fitness and Recreation Tickets Information for Arrow left icon Back Current Students Faculty and Staff Families Alumni Find a Degree Find People Apply Visit Give News Log in Search icon Search Menu Search the site Search icon Close icon Office of Fellowship Advising Arrow up icon Hide Fordham Menu Menu for Office of Fellowship Advising Arrow down icon About Us Message from the Director Our Team Contact Us More About Fellowships Asking for Letters of Recommendation FAQ Guidelines for Recommenders Find Scholarships and Fellowships Alphabetical Listing of Fellowships and Awards For First-Years For Sophomores For Juniors For Seniors For Graduate Students For Alumni Summer Opportunities Opportunities for Non-U.S. Citizens Campion Institute Fellowships Fellowship Awardees New Awardees Recent Awardees News Archives Office of Fellowship Advising The Campion Institute At the Office of Fellowship Advising, we connect students with opportunities. Explore Funding Opportunities View Awardees A fellowship or award is a scholarship that can fund you to do exciting things that will enhance your college experience and more! A fellowship can enrich your college experience with opportunities such as: Conduct Research in Your Field Serve Your Community Study Abroad Attend Graduate School Fordham Recognized as a Fulbright Top Producer for Second Year in a Row With 15 awardees in 2024-2025, Fordham has again been recognized by the U.S. Department of State's Bureau of Educational and Cultural Affairs as a Top Producing Institution -- a result of the wrap-around support our faculty and advisors provide. Our 15 alumni are serving as cultural ambassadors in 12 countries on four continents, from Ghana to the Slovak Republic to Taiwan ! Read Full Article Learn More Two Fordham Students Named Goldwater Scholars for the Second Consecutive Year! Two Fordham juniors—Ashley Clemente and Amrita Das—were chosen to receive the Goldwater Scholarship, the most prestigious national award for undergraduates pursuing STEM research. Read the Full Story Arrow right icon Everyone Can Apply Are you active in an extracurricular club or activity? Are you passionate about creating positive change in your community? Everyone can apply–undergraduates and graduate students, alumni, academic achievers and enthusiastic learners, dedicated leaders and energetic volunteers. Eligibility varies by fellowship and there is a wide range of awards available, addressing a variety of subjects that attract a variety of students. You don't have to be at the top of your class to receive an award. And the process of applying itself is valuable. You will learn how to write about yourself and articulate your plans for the future–skills that will help you apply for internships, jobs and/or graduate school later. Due Dates Thursday June 17 - Rhodes/Marshall candidacy due date Wednesday July 1 - Fulbright first campus due date Monday August 3 - Fulbright second campus due date Tuesday October 6 - Fulbright national due date Events Can't wait for our next event? Schedule a meeting with us at [email protected] . Latest from Fordham Now Arrow left icon Previous Arrow right icon Next ‘People Want to Work’: Student Helping Displaced Ukrainians Earns Prestigious Obama-Chesky Award A Fordham junior involved in fundraising and political activism to support Ukraine and its displaced citizens has been awarded the Obama-Chesky Voyager Scholarship to advance her career in public service. … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon 9 Fordham Grads Earn Fulbright Scholarships Nine Fordham graduates have been awarded Fulbright scholarships that will take them across the globe for research, graduate study, and teaching that fosters cross-cultural exchange and understanding.  This year’s Fordham … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Two Fordham Students Earn Goldwater Scholarship for STEM Research For the third year in a row, two Fordham students have been awarded the Goldwater Scholarship, the most prestigious national award for undergraduates pursuing STEM research. As 2026 Goldwater Scholars, … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon 2 Fordham Students Earn Gilman Scholarships to Study Abroad Two Fordham undergraduates will be heading abroad next year, thanks to a U.S. State Department scholarship that provides support for students studying internationally. Andrra Kryeziu, an honors student in her … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Student Earns Obama-Chesky Scholarship for Public Service, a Fordham First A teenage passion for environmentalism has led one Fordham student to a prestigious scholarship. Lillian Hertel, an honors student double-majoring in political science and environmental studies, is the first Ram … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon ROTC Student Earns Critical Language Scholarship to Study in Japan This summer, rising junior Thomas Monroe is diving headfirst into the language, culture, and daily life of Okayama, Japan, thanks to a scholarship from the U.S. State Department. A psychology … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon 9 Fordham Grads Awarded Fulbright Scholarships Nine recent graduates earned Fulbright scholarships this academic year, carrying on Fordham’s longstanding traditions of cross-cultural exchange and service to others. The Fulbright US Student Program is a highly prestigious … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Fordham’s First ThinkSwiss Scholar Heads to Basel to Research Cancer Treatments Julia Gudis is using her summer vacation to make a positive impact—researching innovative brain tumor treatments in Switzerland.  Gudis is the first Fordham student to earn the ThinkSwiss Research Scholarship, … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon 11 Students Earn Gilman Scholarships for International Study Eleven Fordham undergraduates will be embarking on educational opportunities across the globe, thanks to a State Department scholarship that helps students of limited financial means study abroad.  The Benjamin A. … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Truman Scholarship Awarded to Fordham Student Aiming for Mental Health Career Fordham junior Laura Rosado Philippi has been chosen for a Truman Scholarship, the nation’s most prestigious award for students preparing for careers in public service. She is one of 54 … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Students Awarded Prestigious Goldwater Scholarship for STEM Research Two Fordham juniors—Ashley Clemente and Amrita Das—were chosen to receive the Goldwater Scholarship, the most prestigious national award for undergraduates pursuing STEM research. It’s the second consecutive time that two … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon We’re Here to Help We will guide you through the entire process Whether that’s searching for a fellowship that fits your goals; drafting application essays; or preparing for interviews with selection committees. It's our job to make sure you have all the support you need. Start Early It’s never too early to get started You’ll want plenty of time to prepare your application and increase your chances of receiving an award, so contact us now! Click here to access our Intake Form. A-Z List Scholarship and Fellowship Opportunities Click here to access our full listing. Refer a Student A place for Fordham faculty to refer a student Click here to refer a student. Fellowship News Arrow left icon Previous Arrow right icon Next Humanity In Action: An Interview with April Gore The Humanity in Action Fellowship is an international program aimed at bringing together passionate young people from diverse backgrounds to explore issues regarding human rights, social justice, and democratic values. HIA’s goal is to equip the leaders of tomorrow with the knowledge, skills, and networks they need to promote equality and combat systemic issues. Fellows... Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Study Abroad and the Gilman Scholarship: Emily Lai Emily Lai is a recent graduate of Fordham University Lincoln Center. She graduated with a Bachelor of Arts in Political Science with a minor in Mandarin Chinese. Emily plans to pursue a career in real estate law. She enjoys playing table tennis and golf, playing video games, and baking!  I was excited to talk with... Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Tanzania Through a Screen: Seana Epley’s Virtual CLS Experience By: Melina Piatti-Chayan Through the Critical Language Scholarship, Seana Epley traveled to Tanzania twice–in 2020 and 2021. But both times she traveled virtually. Rather than being located physically in Tanzania for 8-10 weeks, Seana engaged in Tanzanian culture and learned Swahili through her laptop screen. Despite the unique circumstance, Seana embraced it with open arms:... Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Fordham Rams Awarded Fulbright Scholarships Another year, another set of Fulbrighters! The Office of Prestigious Fellowships is happy to announce that several Rams have been awarded scholarships for 2022-2023.  The Fulbright U.S. Student Program is a scholarship created by the U.S. government after World War II in hopes of establishing altruism between nations. Fulbright recipients are usually enthusiastic undergraduates or... Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Fulbrighter in Taiwan: Mobeen Ahmed By Melina Piatti-Chayan Mobeen Ahmed is a graduate student at the University of Chicago and a recipient of the Fulbright U.S. Student Award. As a student undergoing this Fulbright track, Mobeen is working with advisers and institutions of higher education in Taiwan. Prior to this work, Mobeen attended Fordham University at Lincoln Center, where he... Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Q&A with NYC Teaching Fellow Mayarita Castillo By Alex Finn-Atkins Mayarita, can you please tell us a little about yourself?  Sure! I am a Fordham College Lincoln Center (FCLC) ’16 alumna. While at Fordham, I double majored in applied mathematics and Spanish studies. My senior thesis for the honors program was a mathematical and sociological analysis of the intergenerational educational attainment of... Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Margaret Fahey: Fulbright English Teaching Assistant to France Can you tell us about yourself? Have you always been interested in France and French culture? I came to Fordham as a transfer student during my sophomore year. While at Fordham, I studied French and International Political Economy (IPE). Outside of class, I enjoyed working with the FCRH French Club, as this experience allowed me... Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Gabrielle McGovern on Applying to Fulbright: 8 Tips for Success Writing essays for fellowship applications is no easy task. Just ask Gabrielle McGovern, a recipient of the Fulbright grant, who just returned from her year teaching English in Costa Rica. Prior to living la pura vida, this Fordham alumna spent the summer before the Fulbright application deadline writing, revising, editing…and storytelling! While developing what felt... Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Mahbuba Hossain: Becoming an NYC Urban Fellow Receiving my acceptance email from the NYC Urban Fellows Program was the happiest news I could get in what would be the beginning of a very uncertain time. The fall semester of my senior year at Fordham was overwhelming because it had seemed like everyone else in my graduating class had already accepted their full-time... Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Rosalyn Kutsch: Global Classrooms ETA to Spain I’m Rosalyn Kutsch (Fordham ‘19), and I’ve just returned from living in Madrid as a 2019-20 recipient of a Fulbright English Teaching Assistant (ETA) award to Spain. At Fordham Rose Hill, I studied International Political Economy and Latin American and Latino Studies and was involved with the Model United Nations club, which eventually led me... Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Contact the Office of Fellowship Advising Thebaud Hall 106 Rose Hill Campus Lowenstein Hall 806A Lincoln Center Campus Email: [email protected] Phone: 718-817-2774 Connect With Us X logo Instagram logo Explore our programs › Visit us › Apply now › More on social media Helpful Links University Directory Careers at Fordham Nondiscrimination Policy Accessibility Privacy Policy Visit Campus Tours Maps and Directions Virtual Tour"
