ealth sector to speed the search for new treatments, how do we keep it from being used to make bioweapons—viruses, toxins, bacteria, and … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon How Do Our Siblings Help Raise Us? Our parents raise us, yes, but our siblings have an influence too—a fact that science hasn’t spent a lot of time exploring, according to a study co-authored by Fordham psychology … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon 6 Fordham Women Reflect on their Mentors In honor of Women’s History Month, we asked female faculty and staff members to name a woman who helped shape their careers. Their mentors included the pioneering Supreme Court justice … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon What’s on My Desk: Lauren Kopajtic Like many philosophy professors, Lauren Kopajtic, PhD, fills her office with objects that reflect her discipline—but she may be the only one with philosophy-themed Barbie dolls.  Step inside her Collins … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon For Women, By Women: Research That Matters As the nation marks Women’s History Month, women across disciplines at Fordham are engaged in research that serves women on multiple fronts—studying cancer and menopause, exploring how to support women’s … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon A Fordham Focus on AI: Applying Lessons from the Past For our series, A Fordham Focus on AI, we’re speaking with faculty experts from a range of disciplines about the impact of this rapidly evolving technology and what to expect … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon What’s on My Desk: Christina Greer Christina Greer, PhD, is often called on by national media to break down the complexities of American politics. But step into her office at Lincoln Center, and you’ll find a … Read The Full Story Arrow right icon Explore our programs › Visit us › Apply now › More on social media Helpful Links University Directory Careers at Fordham Nondiscrimination Policy Accessibility Privacy Policy Visit Campus Tours Maps and Directions Virtual Tour"
